ng hand. The opponent has been passively calling my bets throughout, suggesting a medium-strength hand like a pair or two pair. The board doesn't show obvious straight or flush possibilities that I should fear greatly. A value bet of 400 chips allows me to extract value from worse hands while not overcommitting if opponent has the rare straight. This sizing is consistent with my previous betting pattern and gives opponent reasonable odds to call with worse hands.\n\nAnswer: 400"}
